 "note": "Awards named in three governor releases (the October release for 22 hospitals, 7 clinically integrated network and innovation-hub awardees and 6 maternal-care awardees; Ohio University; the pharmacy initiative). Amounts are as printed. They do not add up to the October release's headline buckets ($31.4 million for networks and hubs, $30.3 million for maternal care): the listed network and hub awards total $62,020,466 and maternal awards $33,980,000. The release explains that Ohio was awarded $92 million in each of FY2026 and FY2027 for the network and hub initiative and that the announcement includes all of the FY2026 funding and a portion of FY2027, so these amounts span two budget years and the share of the Year 1 award is not computed. The 22 hospitals each received $1,377,479 (the release states the per-hospital amount)."
